  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 145 PM CDT Sun Sep 20 2026\n\nHigh pressure will skirt along the US-Canada border and east of the \nGreat Lakes with time. As a result, Iowa will keep an easterly \nfetch. Upper-level ridging will keep us dry until it's broken down \nat the end of the week. Until we get there, the main theme this week \nwill be partly cloudy skies and highs in the 60s, a timely pattern \nchange for the autumnal equinox. A couple of disturbances will move \nonshore and set up an active weather pattern for next weekend with \nrain chances inching their way into western Iowa.",
